6. Derived Binary Artifact: include/kudroid/framework_dex_bytes.h
===============================================================================
The header file include/kudroid/framework_dex_bytes.h is a compiled binary
artifact generated by compiling all Java sources in framework/ into a single
Dalvik Executable (framework.dex) using D8/R8 and embedding the resulting byte
stream.

It is a combined work containing compiled representations of:
- KuDroid MIT framework stubs and shims
- AOSP Apache-2.0 framework classes
- Apache Harmony Apache-2.0 math, regex, text, and calendar classes
- OpenJDK GPLv2+CPE utility and concurrency classes
- Kotlin Apache-2.0 standard library core classes
- Apache-2.0 HTTP components included by the framework build

Each component retains its license in the DEX and embedded representation; the
header as a whole is not offered under MIT alone. These same terms apply to
executables, IPAs and exported launchers containing the embedded framework.

Binary distributors must retain the applicable notices and license texts and
provide the complete corresponding source for the GPL-covered portions,
including local modifications and the scripts controlling their compilation,
as required by GPLv2 section 3. A generic repository link or moving the DEX to
a separate file does not by itself satisfy these requirements. See
docs/licensing.md for the release procedure and component boundaries.

